    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1026" root="اكل" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَأْكُولٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَكِيلٌ</span>: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُكُلٌ</span>: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَكِيلَةٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  (assumed tropical:)  The <i>subjects</i> of a king. (Z, K, TA.)
Hence the trad., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَأْكُولٌ حِمْيَرَ خَيْرٌ مِنْ آكِلِهَا</span>
(tropical:)  <i>The subjects of Himyer are better than their
king,</i> or <i>ruler.</i> (Z, TA.)

